  "worked_solution": "The polar curve $r=9$ is a circle of radius $9$ centered at the origin. It crosses the positive $y$-axis where $r=9$ and $\\theta =\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14095706/assets/612ca0c41bb3a7ddef6eb02899b6032129c5b23a4ceac650942194990b87bb89.png)\n\nTherefore, the point of intersection in polar coordinates is $(9,\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\,).$",
